{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["And the reason for <b>and you shall keep My covenant</b>: the covenant which I cut with your fathers to be a God to them and to their seed after them (Genesis 17:7). And R. Abraham Ibn Ezra said (on Exodus 19:5): the covenant that Moses will cut with Israel after the giving of the Torah, as it says (Exodus 24:8), 'Behold the blood of the covenant which YHWH has cut with you concerning all these matters.' And by way of truth, that you shall keep My covenant to cleave to Me — (Exodus 23:22), 'But if you will indeed hearken to His voice and do all that I speak.'" "<b>And you shall be to Me a treasure from all the peoples</b> — that you shall be a treasure in My hand, like a coveted thing that the king will not surrender into the hand of another, as in 'and the treasure of kings and of the provinces' (Ecclesiastes 2:8). And He said <b>for all the earth is Mine</b>, in the sense of 'which YHWH apportioned to all the peoples, but you has YHWH taken' (Deuteronomy 4:19–20). And thus He said, 'And I have separated you from the peoples to be Mine' (Leviticus 20:27). Or 'segullah' may mean cleaving, for the earth called 'kol' is Mine, as I explained concerning the verse, 'And YHWH had blessed Abraham in all' (Genesis 24:1) — and the enlightened will understand. And likewise <b>and you shall be to Me</b> (Exodus 19:6), that you shall be Mine in unification, and not like the rest of the peoples. And thus they said in the Mekhilta (ad loc.): <b>and you shall be to Me</b> — as it were, I do not establish and I do not appoint over you any but Me; and thus it says, 'Behold He who guards Israel neither slumbers nor sleeps' (Psalms 121:4)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {0 "The citation of Ibn Ezra gives the verse reference in Arabic numeral format within the Hebrew source; retained as in source."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:10:48.423758167Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}